  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115612",
      "title": "Understanding & Configuring View Encapsulation",
      "lectureOrder": 112,
      "videoOrder": 106,
      "sourceHash": "a28c01148410287d6c37e09b516e0837af6db76d6f5f484cd960184fee09edaf",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 3.18,
          "en": "Now I wanna dive into additional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.18,
          "end": 6.09,
          "en": "Angular features about which you should know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.09,
          "end": 8.883,
          "en": "by fixing this control component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.29,
          "end": 12.75,
          "en": "In the control component CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.75,
          "end": 16.89,
          "en": "I'm looking for the control class on elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.89,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "and then I'm trying to style labels, inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 24.15,
          "en": "and text areas that are nested inside of an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.15,
          "end": 26.64,
          "en": "with the class control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.64,
          "end": 28.24,
          "en": "Well, they offer what we could",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.363,
          "end": 34.17,
          "en": "and should do to fix this broken look of this form is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.17,
          "end": 37.56,
          "en": "we should go to the control component HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.56,
          "end": 40.11,
          "en": "And there on the paragraph we can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.11,
          "end": 41.973,
          "en": "this control clause.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.2,
          "end": 48.2,
          "en": "With that if we do that, it's fixed to some extent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.02,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "The label looks better now, which is a start, but the input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 56.85,
          "en": "and text area isn't looking the way it should look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.85,
          "end": 59.59,
          "en": "It doesn't look horrible, but it doesn't have the look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.701,
          "end": 62.34,
          "en": "it should have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.34,
          "end": 64.92,
          "en": "And why is that the case?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.92,
          "end": 67.953,
          "en": "After all, we have this rule here, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.78999999999999,
          "end": 73.78999999999999,
          "en": "Well yes, but with this CSS rule, we are trying to style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.869,
          "end": 78.72,
          "en": "inputs and text areas that are inside of an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.72,
          "end": 80.82300000000001,
          "en": "with the class control on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.75,
          "end": 84.487,
          "en": "And you might say that's the case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.487,
          "end": 85.62,
          "en": "because we project inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.62,
          "end": 90.18,
          "en": "and text areas here in place of this NG content element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.18,
          "end": 94.05,
          "en": "and therefore they will be inside of an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.05,
          "end": 96.57,
          "en": "with a class of control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.57,
          "end": 101.1,
          "en": "So these styles here should become active on them, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.1,
          "end": 102.47999999999999,
          "en": "Yeah, almost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.47999999999999,
          "end": 107.47999999999999,
          "en": "The problem is Angular does not care about which content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.55,
          "end": 112.55,
          "en": "might eventually end up in your components template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.65,
          "end": 117.65,
          "en": "It only cares about what it sees in your component template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.08,
          "end": 121.872,
          "en": "and there it just sees a placeholder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.872,
          "end": 125.79,
          "en": "not the actual inputs or text areas that will end up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.79,
          "end": 126.843,
          "en": "in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.07,
          "end": 132.51,
          "en": "And that's why these styles won't affect the inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 132.51,
          "end": 135.99,
          "en": "and text areas that will be projected into this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.99,
          "end": 137.553,
          "en": "and into this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 138.63,
          "end": 141.39,
          "en": "So what can we do about that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141.39,
          "end": 146.39,
          "en": "Well you can disable the scoping of these styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 147.15,
          "end": 152.15,
          "en": "here for example, because by default, as I explained,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 152.28,
          "end": 155.34,
          "en": "component styles are scoped to the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 155.34,
          "end": 157.34,
          "en": "to which they belong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 157.34,
          "end": 159.61,
          "en": "They can't affect anything else anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 160.779,
          "end": 162.06,
          "en": "in any other component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 162.06,
          "end": 166.74,
          "en": "But here I actually wanna have these styles affect inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 166.74,
          "end": 171.15,
          "en": "and text areas that are somewhere else in the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 171.15,
          "end": 174.42000000000002,
          "en": "And therefore what we should do here or what we could do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.42000000000002,
          "end": 177.046,
          "en": "to fix this problem is go to the component selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 177.046,
          "end": 178.827,
          "en": "of the control component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 178.827,
          "end": 182.065,
          "en": "and add a new setting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 182.065,
          "end": 184.68,
          "en": "And the new setting you want to add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 184.68,
          "end": 188.305,
          "en": "is the encapsulation setting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 188.305,
          "end": 193.305,
          "en": "And encapsulation takes a value of type view encapsulation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 196.17000000000002,
          "end": 198.72,
          "en": "And that is actually a so-called enum,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.72,
          "end": 202.41,
          "en": "which is essentially a collection of possible values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 202.41,
          "end": 205.685,
          "en": "It's a TypeScript feature which is used by Angular here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.685,
          "end": 210.685,
          "en": "You can and should import view encapsulation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 210.93,
          "end": 215.7,
          "en": "from Angular core and then by adding a dot here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 215.7,
          "end": 219.846,
          "en": "you can access the different values you can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 219.846,
          "end": 223.62,
          "en": "Now emulated would be the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 223.62,
          "end": 226.02,
          "en": "and you don't need to set it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 226.02,
          "end": 231.02,
          "en": "Emulated means that Angular emulates the ShadowDom behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 231.57,
          "end": 235.29,
          "en": "which is a browser thing, which in the end means that styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 235.29,
          "end": 238.89,
          "en": "that belong to a component or to an element should be scoped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 238.89,
          "end": 240.54,
          "en": "to that element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 240.54,
          "end": 243.37,
          "en": "The ShadowDom is not a TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 244.906,
          "end": 245.993,
          "en": "or Angular specific feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 247.025,
          "end": 248.406,
          "en": "Instead it's a browser feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 248.406,
          "end": 249.72,
          "en": "because in the browser you can also build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 249.72,
          "end": 253.95,
          "en": "custom HTML elements totally without Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 253.95,
          "end": 257.07,
          "en": "And Angular emulates that browser feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 257.07,
          "end": 258.753,
          "en": "for its own components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 259.8,
          "end": 263.25,
          "en": "Alternatively, you could choose ShadowDom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 263.25,
          "end": 266.61,
          "en": "so that Angular under the hood uses the real",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 266.61,
          "end": 268.98,
          "en": "browser ShadowDom feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 268.98,
          "end": 271.62,
          "en": "which is not supported by all browsers though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.62,
          "end": 274.971,
          "en": "which is why emulated is the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.971,
          "end": 277.68,
          "en": "But here we need none,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.68,
          "end": 282.18,
          "en": "which simply disables that style scoping.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 282.18,
          "end": 286.81,
          "en": "that style encapsulation as Angular calls it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 286.81,
          "end": 291.81,
          "en": "With that setting added here to this control component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 292.05,
          "end": 297.05,
          "en": "the styles set up here will again become global styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 297.513,
          "end": 302.01,
          "en": "and therefore now they will affect the input and text area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 302.01,
          "end": 305.707,
          "en": "that is eventually rendered into this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 305.707,
          "end": 309.69,
          "en": "And that's therefore another important feature to know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 309.69,
          "end": 312.805,
          "en": "You will typically not need to disable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 312.805,
          "end": 315.06,
          "en": "encapsulation that often,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 315.06,
          "end": 318.39,
          "en": "but if you do need to, like here in this example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 318.39,
          "end": 319.953,
          "en": "this is how you can do it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
